# dracut, target native: dracut-install alone, the one kernelbuild runs with the dracut of the sysroot
### The shell scripts and the modules of dracut are the ones of the image (lfs/dracut), run by the
### bash of the host; dracut-install copies the files they name from the sysroot and resolves the
### libraries of the target binaries reading their ELF headers, so the host needs no emulation.
### The libsystemd >= 257 of the host (systemd-devel) gives it the JSON support, with which the
### modules follow the dlopen dependencies systemd declares (libseccomp, libaudit...): the check
### asks for it, so a host without it rebuilds this package on every run
PKG_DEPS="lfs/kmod:native"
PKG_CHECK="[ x\$( ${INSTALL_EXECPREFIX}/bin/dracut-install --version 2>/dev/null || true ) == x${PKG_VER} ] && ${INSTALL_EXECPREFIX}/bin/dracut-install --json-supported > /dev/null 2>&1"
